  "question": {
    "text": "At a certain depth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;below surface of earth,&nbsp;value of acceleration due to gravity becomes four times that of its value at a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></math> above earth surface. Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is Radius of earth (Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>). The depth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
